{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>וְהֵמַתָּה וגו׳ כְּאִישׁ אֶחָד וגו׳.</b> He revealed his intention upon him, peace be upon him, in this — that he does not ask that HaShem forgive the sin, but only that it not lead to desecration of the Name. And he alluded in his words that the outcry that would draw down what is stated in his words would be only if He kills them כְּאִישׁ אֶחָד, but little by little the matter would not be noticed. And so we find that HaShem did." "<b>וְאָמְרוּ הַגּוֹיִם וגו׳.</b> Meaning, not Egypt alone, but all the nations who heard Your fame — <b>לֵאמֹר</b>, meaning, an expression of exaltation and loftiness of the height of YHWH's power — now they will say ״מִבִּלְתִּי״ וגו׳, and the sanctification of the Name will turn into desecration, heaven forbid, on the lips of all the peoples. And therefore he was precise in saying <b>וְאָמְרוּ</b> with the addition of the vav, to say that besides Egypt etc., also all the nations. A further reason for his saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b>: since the formulation of the words spoken by the nations and their arrangement is not known, therefore he said ״וְאָמְרוּ״ — an saying whose intent is to say ״מִבִּלְתִּי״ וגו׳. He further said <b>לֵאמֹר</b>, meaning, even though they themselves would not justify the matter in their own minds, nevertheless they would say what is entailed by the deed — and this is the measure of the matter: ״וְאָמְרוּ״ וגו׳, and this matter involves only speech alone and not justification of the matter in their minds."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:01.540919479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}